---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmergenceHeader from '../components/EmergenceHeader.astro';
import EmergenceFooter from '../components/EmergenceFooter.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Run a Node — The Emergence Institute"
  description="Join the Lattice mesh in 15 minutes. No blockchain. No crypto wallet. Just a computer and a command line."
>
  <EmergenceHeader slot="header" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label gold">Get Started</p>
      <h1>Run a Node</h1>
      <p class="subtitle-text"><em>You're the missing input. Here's how to join.</em></p>
      <div class="divider"></div>

      <p class="intro">
        The Lattice is a mesh of sovereign nodes. Right now there are two — both run by
        the founder. The mesh correctly produces nothing at this size, because contribution
        requires a third party. <strong>You're the third party.</strong>
      </p>

      <p class="intro">
        This takes about 15 minutes. You need a computer with internet access — a laptop,
        a Raspberry Pi, a cloud VM, anything that runs Linux or macOS. No crypto wallet.
        No blockchain. No signup.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Step 1: Install Rust</h2>

      <div class="step-block">
        <p>You need the Rust compiler. If you already have it, skip ahead.</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <pre><code>curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p class="step-note">Follow the prompts. Choose the default installation. When it finishes, run:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <pre><code>source "$HOME/.cargo/env"</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Step 2: Clone the Repository</h2>

      <div class="step-block">
        <div class="code-block">
          <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/djsph001/lattice-node.git
cd lattice-node</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Step 3: Build</h2>

      <div class="step-block">
        <p>This takes a few minutes the first time. Subsequent builds are fast.</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <pre><code>cargo build --release</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p class="step-note">
          If you're on a low-memory machine (like a Pi), add <code>CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1</code>
          before the command to avoid running out of RAM.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Step 4: Start Your Node</h2>

      <div class="step-block">
        <p>One command. The node generates a persistent identity, connects to the relay, and joins the mesh.</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <pre><code>./target/release/lattice-node \
  --name your-name-here \
  --port 0 \
  --listen-addr 0.0.0.0 \
  --identity-dir ~/.lattice \
  --storage-dir ./lattice-storage \
  --bootstrap-peer /ip4/167.233.223.174/tcp/4001</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p class="step-note">
          <code>--port 0</code> picks a random available port.
          <code>--name</code> is whatever you want to call your node — it shows up in logs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Step 5: Verify You're Connected</h2>

      <div class="step-block">
        <p>Look for these lines in the output. If you see them, you're on the mesh:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <pre><code>Connection established peer=12D3KooWBoVfr...
Identify: peer supports relay (HOP_PROTOCOL)
Kademlia routing table: peer added
Status response received from=relay-hub</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          You should also see heartbeats arriving from relay-hub every 10 seconds,
          and your node's identity line: <code>Node identity established peer_id=...</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What Happens Now</h2>

      <div class="step-block">
        <p>
          Your node is running and peered. The economic layer is active — the
          receipt-gated mint is running — but it correctly produces 0 DUUs because
          there's no third party whose traffic you could relay. <strong>Relaying is a
          three-party act.</strong> Someone originates a message, you carry it, someone
          else receives it. With three nodes, real relay work happens for the first time.
        </p>

        <p>
          When a fourth person joins, the mesh crosses the threshold where quorum
          (3-of-5) becomes possible. Certified contributions begin. Thickness accrues.
          Governance activates. Your node helped make that happen.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>You're not late. You're the third node.</strong> The mesh has been running
          with two — correctly producing nothing — because it was waiting for you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Keeping It Running</h2>

      <div class="step-block">
        <p>
          The node stops when you close the terminal. To keep it running permanently,
          add it as a systemd service (Linux) or launchd agent (macOS). A service file
          is in the repository at <code>deploy/lattice-lumen.service</code> — copy and
          customize it.
        </p>
        <p>
          On restart, your node's identity persists (the key at <code>~/.lattice/identity.key</code>).
          The economic state does not yet persist — this is being built. Until then, a
          restart means starting fresh, which is fine while the mesh is bootstrapping.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What You're Joining</h2>

      <div class="step-block">
        <p>
          The Emergence Institute is building an apparatus for turning multiple vantage
          points into shared truth — without central servers, without a blockchain,
          without requiring anyone to trust the founder. Every mechanism is running
          code in a public repository.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/emergence/architecture">Read the architecture →</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/emergence/constitutional">Read the constitutional design →</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/emergence/protocols">Read the protocol specifications →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Questions?</h2>

      <div class="step-block">
        <p>
          Something didn't work? The build failed? Join the
          <a href="https://discord.gg/emergenceinstitute">Discord</a> and ask.
          The mesh is small enough that you'll get an answer from the person who
          wrote the code.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <EmergenceFooter slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .subtitle-text {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 620px;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .step-block {
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .code-block {
    margin: 1rem 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .code-block pre {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .code-block code {
    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--gold-light);
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .step-note {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .step-note code {
    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--gold-light);
  }

  section h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  section + section {
    border-top: none;
  }
</style>
